        content: "Multiple specialized agents working together can tackle problems no single agent can.\n\n**Why Multi-Agent?**\n- Single agents struggle with very complex tasks\n- Specialized agents are more reliable than generalists\n- Agents can review each other's work (quality control)\n\n**Common Patterns:**\n\n**1. Sequential Pipeline:**\nAgent A → Agent B → Agent C (each handles a stage)\n- Research Agent → Writer Agent → Editor Agent\n\n**2. Debate/Discussion:**\nAgents argue different perspectives to reach better conclusions\n- Pro Agent vs Con Agent → Moderator Agent synthesizes\n\n**3. Hierarchical:**\nManager agent delegates to specialist agents\n- Project Manager → [Researcher, Coder, Designer, Tester]\n\n**4. Collaborative:**\nAgents work in parallel and merge results\n- Multiple research agents each tackle a subtopic\n\n**CrewAI Example:**\n```\nCrew: 'Blog Writing Team'\n- Researcher: Finds facts and data\n- Writer: Creates engaging content\n- Editor: Polishes grammar and flow\n- SEO Specialist: Optimizes for search\n```\n\n**Challenges:**\n- Communication overhead between agents\n- Error propagation (one agent's mistake affects others)\n- Cost (more agents = more API calls)\n- Debugging is complex",
