        content: "Not every AI task needs a massive model. Small Language Models (SLMs) are reshaping the landscape.\n\n**What Are Small Language Models?**\n- Models with 1B-7B parameters (vs 100B+ for frontier models)\n- Examples: Phi-3 (Microsoft), Gemma (Google), Llama 3.2 1B/3B (Meta)\n- Run on laptops, phones, and edge devices\n\n**Why SLMs Matter:**\n1. **Privacy:** Data never leaves your device\n2. **Speed:** Millisecond latency vs seconds for cloud models\n3. **Cost:** Zero API costs after initial setup\n4. **Offline:** Works without internet\n5. **Compliance:** Meets data residency requirements\n\n**Where SLMs Excel:**\n- Text classification and sentiment analysis\n- Summarization of short documents\n- Code completion and simple generation\n- Chatbots for narrow domains\n- Data extraction and formatting\n\n**Edge AI Use Cases:**\n- **Mobile apps:** On-device translation, smart replies\n- **IoT devices:** Voice assistants, anomaly detection\n- **Healthcare:** Patient data processing without cloud\n- **Manufacturing:** Real-time quality inspection\n\n**Quantization:**\nMaking models smaller without losing much quality:\n- FP16 → INT8 → INT4 (progressively smaller and faster)\n- A 7B model at INT4 runs on 4GB RAM\n- Tools: GGUF format, llama.cpp, ONNX Runtime\n\n**The Trend:**\nSmall models are getting better faster than large models are getting cheaper. For many production tasks, a well-tuned 3B model outperforms a general-purpose 70B model.",
        keyTakeaways: ["Small models (1-7B params) run on laptops and phones", "SLMs offer privacy, speed, zero API cost, and offline capability", "Quantization (INT4) makes 7B models run on 4GB RAM", "Well-tuned small models often outperform general large models for specific tasks"]
