        content: "Enterprise-grade AI workflows require sophisticated orchestration patterns.\n\n**Conditional Branching:**\nWorkflows that adapt based on intermediate results:\n```\nInput → AI Classifier → \n  IF 'complaint' → Sentiment Analysis → Escalation Agent\n  IF 'question' → RAG Search → Answer Generator\n  IF 'feedback' → Categorizer → Dashboard Update\n```\n\n**Error Handling & Retry Logic:**\n- **Exponential backoff:** Wait 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s between retries\n- **Fallback chains:** If GPT-4 fails → try Claude → try Gemini\n- **Dead letter queues:** Failed items saved for manual review\n- **Circuit breakers:** Stop calling a failing service temporarily\n\n**Parallel Processing:**\nRun independent AI tasks simultaneously:\n- Translate document into 5 languages at once\n- Analyze 100 resumes in parallel batches\n- Generate images while writing text content\n\n**Human-in-the-Loop Patterns:**\n1. **Approval gates:** AI generates → Human approves → Workflow continues\n2. **Exception handling:** AI flags uncertain cases for human review\n3. **Quality sampling:** Human reviews random 10% for quality assurance\n\n**Monitoring & Observability:**\n- Track success/failure rates per workflow step\n- Measure latency at each stage\n- Monitor token usage and costs\n- Set up alerts for anomalies",
        keyTakeaways: ["Conditional branching makes workflows adaptive and intelligent", "Error handling with retries, fallbacks, and circuit breakers ensures reliability", "Parallel processing dramatically speeds up batch AI operations", "Human-in-the-loop patterns maintain quality at scale"]
