        content: "**Project: Create a Q&A System Over Your Notes**\n\n**Conceptual Exercise (No Coding Required):**\n\n1. **Prepare Your Data:**\n- Take notes from 3 different lectures/chapters\n- Split them into logical chunks (by topic/section)\n- You should have 15-20 chunks\n\n2. **Manual RAG Simulation:**\nFor each question below, manually find the most relevant chunks:\n- 'What is the main concept covered in lecture 2?'\n- 'How do topics from lecture 1 and 3 connect?'\n- 'What examples were given for [specific concept]?'\n\n3. **AI-Powered RAG:**\nUsing the AI Chat in this platform:\n- Paste your notes as context\n- Ask specific questions\n- Compare AI answers with and without your notes as context\n- Note the difference in quality\n\n4. **Design Your RAG System:**\nDocument a RAG architecture for:\n- Input: All your course materials\n- Process: How would you chunk, embed, and retrieve?\n- Output: A study assistant that answers questions from YOUR materials\n\n**Bonus: Code-Based RAG**\nIf you're comfortable with Python:\n- Use LangChain + ChromaDB\n- Load a PDF with PyPDFLoader\n- Split, embed, store, and query\n- Build a simple Streamlit interface"
