        id: "9-3", title: "Fine-Tuning in Practice", duration: "14 min", type: "reading",
        content: "Let's walk through the practical process of fine-tuning a model.\n\n**Fine-Tuning with OpenAI:**\n\n**Step 1: Prepare Data**\n```python\n# Create JSONL training file\ntraining_data = [\n  {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"...\"}, \n                 {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...\"}, \n                 {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"...\"}]}\n  # ... 50+ examples\n]\n```\n\n**Step 2: Upload Training File**\n```python\nfile = client.files.create(\n  file=open(\"training.jsonl\", \"rb\"),\n  purpose=\"fine-tune\"\n)\n```\n\n**Step 3: Start Fine-Tuning**\n```python\njob = client.fine_tuning.jobs.create(\n  training_file=file.id,\n  model=\"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\"\n)\n```\n\n**Step 4: Monitor Progress**\n- Training typically takes 15-60 minutes\n- Monitor loss metrics — should decrease over epochs\n\n**Step 5: Test Your Model**\n```python\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n  model=\"ft:gpt-4o-mini:my-org::abc123\",\n  messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"test question\"}]\n)\n```\n\n**Hyperparameters:**\n- **Epochs:** Number of passes through training data (usually 3-5)\n- **Learning rate:** How fast the model adapts (auto is usually fine)\n- **Batch size:** Examples processed together (auto recommended)\n\n**Evaluation:**\n- Hold out 20% of data for testing\n- Compare fine-tuned model vs base model on test set\n- Check for overfitting: great on training data, poor on new data",
