        id: "10-2", title: "Working with AI APIs", duration: "16 min", type: "reading",
        content: "AI APIs are your building blocks. Here's how to work with them.\n\n**OpenAI API:**\n```javascript\nconst response = await fetch('https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Authorization': `Bearer ${API_KEY}`,\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    model: 'gpt-4o-mini',\n    messages: [{role: 'user', content: 'Hello!'}],\n    max_tokens: 500\n  })\n});\n```\n\n**Key API Concepts:**\n- **Authentication:** API keys (keep secret!)\n- **Rate limits:** Requests per minute/day\n- **Tokens:** Input + output tokens determine cost\n- **Streaming:** Get responses word-by-word for better UX\n- **Error handling:** Retry on 429 (rate limit), handle 500s gracefully\n\n**Cost Management:**\n- Use cheaper models for simple tasks (GPT-4o-mini vs GPT-4o)\n- Cache responses for repeated queries\n- Set max_tokens to limit output length\n- Implement usage tracking per user\n\n**Other Useful APIs:**\n- **Whisper:** Speech-to-text\n- **DALL-E:** Image generation\n- **ElevenLabs:** Voice synthesis\n- **Pinecone:** Vector database\n- **Replicate:** Run open-source models\n\n**Architecture Pattern:**\n```\nFrontend → Your Backend → AI API\n          (auth, caching,\n           rate limiting)\n```\nNever call AI APIs directly from the frontend (exposes API keys).",
        keyTakeaways: ["Always call AI APIs from backend, never frontend", "Cost management: cache, use cheaper models, set token limits", "Handle rate limits (429) and errors gracefully", "Architecture: Frontend → Backend → AI API"]
